fic paths (e.g., /admin/, /private/)</p></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[#00AEEF] text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm font-bold">3</div><p class="text-sm text-[#0F0F0F]/70">Add your sitemap URL (helps search engines discover all your pages)</p></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[#00AEEF] text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm font-bold">4</div><p class="text-sm text-[#0F0F0F]/70">Generate, download, and upload the file to your website&#x27;s root directory</p></div></div></div><div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-50 to-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 md:p-8"><div class="mb-6"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-question-mark w-5 h-5 text-[#00AEEF]" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><path d="M12 17h.01"></path></svg><h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-black">Frequently Asked Questions</h3></div><p class="text-sm md:text-base text-gray-600">Common questions about this tool and how to use it effectively</p></div><div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-4 md:p-6"><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">1</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What is a robots.txt file and why do I need one?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>A robots.txt file is a text file placed in your website's root directory that tells search engine crawlers which pages or sections of your site they can or cannot access. It's essential for controlling crawler behavior, preventing duplicate content indexing, protecting sensitive areas, and managing your crawl budget efficiently.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">2</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">Where should I place the robots.txt file on my website?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>The robots.txt file must be placed in the root directory of your website (e.g., https://example.com/robots.txt). It cannot be placed in a subdirectory or subfolder. Search engines will only look for it at the domain root, and it must be publicly accessible without authentication.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">3</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What do User-agent directives mean and which one should I use?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>User-agent directives specify which crawler bot the rules apply to. Using '*' applies rules to all bots universally. You can also target specific bots like 'Googlebot' for Google or 'Bingbot' for Bing. If you want different rules for different bots, create multiple user-agent sections in your robots.txt file.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">4</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">How do I block specific search engine bots while allowing others?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Create separate user-agent sections for each bot. For example, to block only Bingbot while allowing others, use 'User-agent: Bingbot' followed by 'Disallow: /' to block everything. Then add 'User-agent: *' with specific Allow/Disallow rules for other bots. Each user-agent section works independently.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">5</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">Should I include my sitemap URL in robots.txt?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Yes, including your sitemap URL in robots.txt helps search engines discover all your pages more efficiently. Add it at the end of your file using the format 'Sitemap: https://example.com/sitemap.xml'. You can include multiple sitemap URLs if your site has several sitemaps for different content types.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">6</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">Can I use wildcards in robots.txt path rules?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Yes, you can use wildcards like '*' (matches any sequence of characters) and '$' (matches end of URL). For example, 'Disallow: /*.pdf$' blocks all PDF files, and 'Disallow: /private*' blocks any URL starting with /private. However, wildcards are not supported by all crawlers, so use them carefully.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0" ><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">7</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">How can I test my robots.txt file before deploying it?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Use Google Search Console's robots.txt Tester tool to validate your file and test specific URLs. This tool shows you exactly how Googlebot will interpret your rules and helps identify syntax errors. Always test before deploying to avoid accidentally blocking important pages from search engines.</p></div></div></div><div class="mt-6 text-center" ><p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2">Still have questions?</p><a href="/contact" class="text-[#00AEEF] font-semibold hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm md:text-base">Contact our team for help<svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></section><section class="py-16 bg-white border-t border-gray-100"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-black mb-3" style="font-family:var(--font-heading)">Related Tools You Might Like</h2><p class="text-gray-600 text-lg">Continue optimizing your website with these complementary tools</p></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-8"><a class="group relative bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6 hover:border-[#00AEEF] hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1" href="/tools/robots-validator"><div class="mb-4"><div class="inline-flex p-3 rounded-xl bg-[#00AEEF]/10 group-hover:bg-[#00AEEF] transition-colors"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-shield w-6 h-6 text-[#00AEEF] group-hover:text-white transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z"></path></svg></div></div><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-black mb-2 group-hover:text-[#